WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:02.790
Every day... America moves.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:05.890
And every journey leaves
something in the air.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.400
It wasn't always like this.

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.380
Every way of travelling
built a place to stop.

00:00:12.850 --> 00:00:15.530
A courtyard. An inn. A station.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.950
Then the engine...
and the petrol station.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:21.900
But the electric car
is older than you think.

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.330
It just had to wait for its battery.

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.920
Now it's here.
And the air is beginning to clear.

00:00:30.500 --> 00:00:35.160
Today, more than seven million
electric cars drive on American roads.

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:39.010
One in every ten
new cars sold is electric.

00:00:39.250 --> 00:00:43.180
By twenty-fifty, that share
could increase four times.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:46.610
But a charge still takes
twenty minutes to an hour.

00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:50.350
And today, we spend it
at the edge of a parking lot.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.000
What if the wait became a place?

00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:00.570
A café. A room for the night.
A market. A park.

00:01:01.160 --> 00:01:03.100
A charger at the heart of a building,

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.520
for travellers, for neighbours,
for whole towns.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:15.170
As the cars change, the places
we stop can change with them.

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:18.860
Every one of those cars
will need somewhere to pause.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:27.100
The Powerhouse.
